by now you're probably aware that the  sealed 30 ton black granite sarcophagus  has been opened which was recently  discovered in Alexandria Egypt and made  headlines around the world as everyone  waited to see what would be found inside  and speculation flourished on the  internet and in the news with  suggestions ranging from ancient  Egyptian mummies containing riches and  treasure to the lost remains of  Alexander the Great to even an ancient  curse that would lead to a zombie  apocalypse but what they did find were  the gruesome remains of three mummies or  should I say skulls with their skeletons  along with a disgusting and horrendously  foul odor red sewage which I'll be  discussing and sharing more photos of in  just a moment but first of all there is  way more to this story than the pictures  and the details that were reported by  the news because a few things that they  shared about it just do not add up and  in this video I'm going to connect the  dots and some really interesting  information about this as well as share  additional photos that did make the  headline articles going around the world  on this topic now real quick if you  haven't watched my previous video that I  made before the sarcophagus was opened  be sure to check that out and I'll  include a link pop up at the end of this  video so you can watch it as I discuss  many interesting details that I won't be  mentioning again in this video but one  point that I did make was that the  opening of this sarcophagus should be  done on live TV or through live  streaming which ultimately did not  happen and is a total shame for a  variety of reasons that aside the  process of opening the sarcophagus was  very difficult the pit that it's buried  in is 16 and a half feet or five meters  deep and it's easier to appreciate just  how deep that is when you see pictures  of it and you can see here that they  even tied two ladders together to climb  down into the pit to open the lid which  was sealed with a thick mortar they  utilized wedges to pry it open and then  stack wood in between the lid and the  sarcophagus to elevate it but something  happened as soon as they cracked it open  the smell of the red sewage inside was  so pungent that they had to stop working  and leave the pit in fact the smell was  so bad that at first they thought the  fumes could be lethally toxic  so they put on surgical masks before  we're continuing and in this photo you  can actually see here Mustafa Waziri the  secretary-general of Egypt Supreme  Council of Antiquities being the very  first person to look and see what's  inside this massive stone box and this  here is what he saw the pool of a red  colored sewage that they claimed must  have leaked into the sarcophagus at some  point after it was buried so at this  time they decided to completely remove  the massive 15 tonne lid and when I say  massive you have to compare it to the  size of people to truly appreciate it  but the whole sarcophagus itself  measures nearly nine feet long five and  a half feet wide and six feet tall and  you can see the metric conversion here  in this photo but to lift and remove the  lid they of course to use heavy  machinery a crane to do so and just look  at this lid isn't that thing amazing of  course in my prior video I discussed the  issues involved with cutting and carving  this black granite stone and how bronze  saws as theorized by Egyptologists and  archeologists could not have done this  especially not with this level of  precision and I also mentioned how  archaeologists suggest that ropes and  pulleys were used by the ancients to  lift or lower heavy stones and although  I do not doubt the use of police by the  ancients it must be mentioned that no  police or ropes have ever been found  from the ancient Egyptians that were  large enough or strong enough to have  sustained this level of weight but that  of course does not mean that they didn't  exist either but it's just important for  everyone to see what it takes in modern  times to lift something of this weight a  massive freakin hydraulic crane and  while we're at it look at the  surroundings of where this was found in  the middle of the densely populated city  of Alexandria Egypt so it of course  makes you wonder what else could be  buried in the immediate area around it  what is hidden just meters underneath  these buildings here and don't forget  that this sarcophagus was discovered by  accident by a construction crew working  on a new building but getting back to  the red sewage that was found inside the  sarcophagus it must be mentioned that in  the three weeks since the discovery and  prior to opening it there was no smell  or evidence of sewage within the pit we  all remember the considerable amount of  speculation about what could be hidden  inside and not one single person  involved with this discovery said  anything  about the smell of death emitting from  the sealed box and this not forgets that  they were very specific in stating that  the lid was sealed with thick mortar so  wait a second if sewage was somehow able  to leak into this sealed sarcophagus at  some point which is exactly what they  stated about it why then couldn't they  smell it until after the lid had already  been opened I mean they specifically  stated that it wasn't until after they  pried open the lid that they could smell  it and again we can see that before it  was open nobody was wearing masks and  once they crapped it open they all did I  mean I wasn't there so I obviously do  not know all the details involved but  what makes them so sure that this sewage  came from outside and leaked its way in  because it seems to me that this red  sewage is actually what's left of the  decayed bodily fluids of the three  individuals that they found inside they  of course pumped the fluid out and when  they did this is what you could see  absolutely disgusting right what you're  looking at are the skeletal remains of  three individuals and here are the other  photos provided by Egyptian antiquities  where you can see it from above and also  photos of the three skulls that they  pulled from it so there's a few things  to discuss about this first is that the  only thing inside were the bones and the  fluid nothing else no clothing no  jewelry just bones and sewage and you  can see that came from two different  sources so it sounds like these three  people were essentially naked when they  were put into this box and well I'll  discuss more about that in a second but  Mustafa Waziri also clarified that none  of the mummies belong to the Ptolemaic  period which is about 2300 years ago as  was previously suggested particularly  due to the alabaster head found not far  from this sarcophagus it's been  suggested that the three individuals  could have been warriors or soldiers  during the time of the Pharaohs and they  suggest this due to the trauma to one of  the skulls found which could be from an  arrow through the head obviously this is  all speculation it could be true but we  really have no idea because there was  nothing found in the stone box other  than the bones and what I believe to be  the leftover and decayed bodily fluids  of these three naked dead  people found inside of it additionally  there were no inscriptions or works of  art of any kind within the box or  outside of it which is actually highly  unusual and here you can see a similar  example of a sarcophagus of this kind  and all the incredible hieroglyphs found  both in and outside of it so there are  none found on the newly discovered  sarcophagus and yet various news outlets  are still suggesting that the box is  from the Ptolemaic period which is  certainly ridiculous  it's beyond clear that this box was  reused and the three people found inside  were not the original person or things  meant for it one thing that stood out to  me were the skulls at least one of them  appears to be a bit small and I am by no  means an expert on skeletal remains and  it was actually suggested that this was  perhaps a family burial but maybe these  were young adults a female who knows but  again these people were apparently  buried naked and left with no type of  inscription or marker of any kind on  their grave which is a bit suspicious I  can't help but think that perhaps three  people went missing thousands of years  ago and someone got rid of the bodies in  a way that nobody should ever find them  I mean think about it they were murdered  and dumped naked into the stone box and  it was sealed up the remains are  actually now being moved to the  Alexandria national restoration Museum  where they will be examined to identify  cause of death and possible age and the  sarcophagus is being sent to a military  museum so here is something that you're  pretty much guaranteed to find  disgusting / disturbing remember that  red sewage that they found inside guess  what they decided to do with it they  kept some samples of it to be analyzed  and the rest was literally dumped into  the street and you can actually watch  video of it here on YouTube and you can  even tell when watching it that this  guy's face wreaked of guilt and the  people watching and taking photos around  him and although they were speaking  Arabic and I couldn't understand it it  seemed that they were giving this guy's  [ __ ] for doing what he was doing I mean  pouring the foul liquid remains of human  bodies into the street around their  homes there are so many things wrong  with this and besides the fact that it's  an obvious health issue to the people in  the area but they're also literally  discarding the remain  evidence I don't know how much of this  ancient mummy juice they kept to be  analyzed but this is a profound example  of the reckless negligent behavior on  behalf of the Egyptian antiquities and  excavations do you see what I mean  with all of this said it will be  interesting to see pictures of this  sarcophagus once it is cleaned out but  it really makes you wonder it was  originally inside of it clearly this  thing was reused and there is certainly  way more to the story than meets the eye  I mean think about what an incredible  mystery this is people went to an  incredible extent to cut in carve this  stone block which was more than sixty  six thousand pounds or more than 30  metric tons all to just dump three naked  bodies in it with no inscription of any  kind no no no no there is way more to  this story than meets the eye like I  said earlier and I'm very curious to see  what your thoughts are so definitely  leave me a comment and share what your  insight is on this but I'll leave it at  that hit the like button and subscribe  but I'm Jimmy this is bright insight and  I have many more videos to come and a  whole wide variety of topics take care  of everybody
 

